## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a scalable, governed, multi-region data lake with reliable ingestion, deduplication, and schema evolution.

## Key Concepts

- Regional ingestion paths and Parquet data lake
- Lake Formation governance and CRR
- Idempotent ingestion with event_id dedup
- Schema evolution via Avro + Glue Schema Registry
- Late data handling and e2e testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode dedupe
async function isDuplicate(event_id){
  const exists = await dynamo.get({PK: event_id});
  if (exists) return true;
  await dynamo.put({PK: event_id, ...});
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CRR for thousands of regions?
- How would you monitor data quality drift in this setup?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests diagnosing streaming governance, tenant isolation, schema evolution, and automated remediation in real-time.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant schemas, Glue Schema Registry, data masking, Lake Formation permissions
- Parquet partitioning, Glue Catalog, lineage via EventBridge, testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: mask email/phone in streaming records before land
function maskPII(record) {
  if (!record) return record;
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.user) {
    if (r.user.email) r.user.email = '***@***.com';
    if (r.user.phone) r.user.phone = '******';
  }
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift across tenants? 
- What metrics would you emit for data quality?
